  "sample_note": "sample_identities keeps EVERY row involved in a duplicate under either the single-column or the composite identity, plus up to 20 clean rows per entity. For `agent` that is load-bearing: the composite entry must contain the very rows `id` alone collides, or 'the composite is a key' is proved over rows that never collided. For `message`, at most 4 copies of the repeated empty uuid are kept \u2014 the class is 'this identity repeats', not how many times. `measured` holds the real counts over the full fan-out."
